  "name": "atx-v1/expired-beyond-skew",
  "description": "The baseline-valid.json credential, ATX v1.0, with expiresAt 2026-05-23T23:58:59Z, 61 seconds earlier than the verifier's pinned clock, 2026-05-24T00:00:00Z, and its one Ed25519 signature made over that expiresAt. core.md §1.3 step 2 evaluates expiry within the family clock-skew bound of ATP §10.2: a verifier tolerates at most 60 seconds of clock skew, and the tolerance extends no TTL or cache window. At every tolerance from 0 to 60 seconds the credential is expired, so a verifier MUST REJECT with an expiry reason. A verifier that tolerates more than 61 seconds of skew, outside the bound, wrongly ACCEPTs; expired.json, whose expiresAt is 508 days earlier than the clock, is rejected at any tolerance short of 508 days, so it does not tell such a verifier from one inside the bound. An expiresAt less than 60 seconds before the clock pins no verdict: a verifier with no tolerance rejects it and one with 60 seconds accepts it. 61 seconds is one second past the bound, so the verdict does not turn on whether a verifier holds a credential expired at the instant its expiresAt plus its tolerance equals its clock.",
  "requirement": "§1.3 step 2: expiry is evaluated within the family clock-skew bound of ATP §10.2, at most 60 seconds, so a credential whose expiresAt is 61 seconds earlier than the verifier's clock is rejected at every tolerance the bound allows",
